description: "Format constraints for DevolaFlow SKILL.md and CLAUDE.md — codified from v2.1.0/v2.2.0 iteration lessons"
alwaysApply: true
---

## Rule SF-1 — Line Budget

SKILL.md must stay under 500 lines. Verify with `wc -l` or the `test_skill_md_under_500_lines` integration test before committing changes.

## Rule SF-2 — Required Frontmatter Keys

SKILL.md frontmatter (YAML between `---` delimiters) must include ALL of: `id`, `version`, `purpose`, `triggers`, `tier`, `token_estimate`, `last_updated`, `name`, `description`. The `description` field must describe WHEN/WHY to activate the skill (trigger conditions), not WHAT the skill does (capability summary). This prevents agents from using the description as a compressed substitute for reading the full skill content.

## Rule SF-3 — Version Consistency

The version string must match `src/devolaflow/__init__.py` `__version__` in ALL of these locations:

**Canonical 7 (the ones `scripts/bump_version.py` pattern-replaces):**

1. SKILL.md frontmatter `version:`, banner, and body "Current version:" text (file: `workflow-system/agent/SKILL.md`)
2. `workflow-skill.yaml` identity section
3. `pyproject.toml` version field
4. `scripts/generate_human_docs.py` SOURCE_VERSION
5. `tests/test_smoke.py` version assertion
6. `README.md` badge and version example
7. `workflow-system/human/demo/benchmark-results/index.html` SAMPLE_DATA version

**`.cursor/skills/devola-flow/` project-local mirror (kept in sync bytewise by `scripts/sync_cursor_skill.py`):**

8. `.cursor/skills/devola-flow/SKILL.md` — bytewise mirror of `workflow-system/agent/SKILL.md` (version strings propagate automatically)
9. `.cursor/skills/devola-flow/references/*.md` — 8 bytewise mirrors of `workflow-system/agent/references/*.md`
10. `.cursor/skills/devola-flow/examples/*.md` — 3 bytewise mirrors of `workflow-system/agent/examples/*.md`
11. `.cursor/skills/devola-flow/.devola-flow-version` — single-line stamp equal to `__version__`

The mirror set (12 content files + 1 stamp) is EXACTLY what `scripts/install.sh::install_cursor` downloads for Cursor end-users. Editing the mirror set here requires editing the same list in `scripts/sync_cursor_skill.py` and `scripts/install.sh` in lockstep.

**Workflow:**

```bash
python scripts/bump_version.py <new-version>   # bumps canonical 7 + auto-syncs mirror
make sync-human-docs                            # regenerate EN/ZH human docs
python -m pytest tests/test_version.py -v       # asserts all 11 locations + stamp agree
```

`bump_version.py` invokes `sync_cursor_skill.py` at its final step, so the mirror cannot drift under normal bumps. If you edit `workflow-system/agent/SKILL.md` or any reference/example manually (without bumping), you MUST run `make sync-cursor-skill` before committing. `make all` and `make release-preflight` both include the sync as a safety net.

## Rule SF-4 — Valid Reference Links

Every `references/xxx.md` path mentioned in SKILL.md must correspond to an actual file under `workflow-system/agent/references/`. Do not reference files that do not exist.

Current valid references: `agent-hierarchy.md`, `context-isolation.md`, `decomposition-gate.md`, `execution-protocol.md`, `message-schemas.md`, `meta-framework.md`, `repo-modes.md`, `team-roles.md`.

## Rule SF-5 — No Absolute Paths

SKILL.md, CLAUDE.md, and all reference documents must use relative paths from the repository root. Never use absolute filesystem paths (e.g., `/home/user/...`, `/benchmarks/...`). External resources must be referenced via their remote URL (e.g., `https://github.com/YoRHa-Agents/DevolaFlow`).

## Rule SF-6 — External Resource URLs

When referencing EvoBench, upstream tools, or external benchmarks, always use the remote GitHub repository URL as the canonical reference. Users provide their local clone path at runtime; the SKILL and docs must not assume any local path.
